# Rest while DISEASED: does the rest still heal hit points, and how much ability
# damage does it restore? Read by tools/check_rest_disease.sh. bd inc-d8i7.
# Same route, same traps ('z' lowercase, depth 2, genocide, armour off) as
# rest-poison.keys -- read that header. The check script splices a god from
# tools/fixtures/rest-disease-god.irh whose handler stages one of three cases.
# before/after dump "Examine Player Data": HP line plus the Stati list
# (ADJUST_DMG rows carry Val:A_STR / Mag:-n).

@include chargen.keys
@until "HP:" ESC

# STRIP THE WORN ARMOUR. Since the starting kit arranges a proficient
# character's armour onto its body (bd inc-zzwm), the orc barbarian now sleeps
# in its orcish hide armour, and Player::Rest prints "You take off your armour
# to rest." (and puts it back on waking) -- extra lines that push the wake
# message off the 'woke' screen this check reads. Taking the armour off into
# the pack here, before any game time is spent, restores the route the check
# was written for: no armour to doff or don during the night. 'i' opens the
# inventory, 'j' is the Armour slot letter (src/Managers.cpp:441 SlotLetters;
# SL_ARMOUR is 9), SPACE lifts the suit into the air, 's' stows it in the pack
# (the medium backpack the kit grants), and ESC returns to play.
i
j
SPACE
s
ESC

w y
@choose "Ascend / Descend Depth"
"2" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC

w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
@until "HP:" ESC

w
@choose "Become Divine Champion"
"Rest Disease Test God" ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*10
@dump:before
ESC

z
y
SPACE SPACE
@dump:woke

w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*10
@dump:after
ESC
@quit
